; registry-mismatch — the binary-only registry-identity anchor (T5b).
;
; A nonempty host join with two distinct, same-shaped names (`alpha`,
; `bravo`: both 5 bytes, ncomp 1, registry 0). Each has a keyed track so
; the frames show the join is actually exercised. The harness probes a
; structural change (a valid arity change) and a name swap (ordered names
; only); both PACTs are VALID canonical bytes, so the binary gate is the
; semantic registry-identity refusal (status 1/reason 9), never the
; malformed-PACT status 2. The text path records explicit skips.
(transport :bpm 120 :meter [4 4])

(track :target alpha
  (key :at 0b :value 0.1)
  (key :at 4b :value 0.9))

(track :target bravo
  (key :at 0b :value 0.8)
  (key :at 4b :value 0.2))
